Register the Orca CLI from the web client

Every agent-skill setup card (Orchestration, Browser Use, Computer Use, Linear,
Ephemeral VMs, Mobile Emulator, Settings > CLI) warned "Orca CLI registration is
unavailable" and could never register `orca-ide`.

`createCliApi()` in the web preload was a hardcoded `supported:false` stub,
though the terminal those cards open runs on the connected server where the CLI
exists. Three runtime RPC methods - `cli.getInstallStatus`, `cli.install` and
`cli.remove` - reuse the `CliInstaller` behind the desktop IPC handlers, with
the same shell-path hydration so `pathConfigured` matches what a PTY sees. None
is on `MOBILE_RPC_METHOD_ALLOWLIST`: a paired phone must never register or
remove host commands.

The hydration and the three installer calls move to `src/main/cli/cli-registration.ts`,
following the split upstream performs at v1.4.190 on `ipc/preflight.ts`,
`ipc/ssh.ts` and `ipc/plugins.ts`: the domain logic leaves the handler file and
`ipcMain.handle` stays behind to call it. Reaching them through `ipc/cli.ts`
instead would pull `import { ipcMain } from 'electron'` into the runtime's
import graph, which `config/runtime-electron-baseline.txt` requires to stay
empty.

To test, open Settings > CLI in the tile, register the CLI, then run `orca-ide`
in a terminal on the workspace. `node config/scripts/check-runtime-electron-ratchet.mjs`
must report 0 entries. Red with this patch popped: `web-cli-registration.test.ts`
- the three routed members - and `cli.test.ts`, the family's registration.
`cli-registration.test.ts` and `mobile-rpc-allowlist.test.ts` stay green popped:
the first tests overlay code, the second is a patched file, so popping deletes
its cases rather than failing them. Both are guards, not coverage.
